<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="08">
<name>Heater &amp; Air Conditioner/Ventilation</name>
<section id="1002K_S000B" variety="S000B">
<name>Air Conditioner</name>
<ttl id="1002K_S000B_7421V_T0025" variety="T0025">
<name>Heater &amp; Air Conditioner System</name>
<para id="RM0000005LM00RX" category="C" type-id="30548" name-id="5229F-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B1497/97</dtccode>
<dtcname>BUS IC communication malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005LM00RX_05" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000BZD00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The air conditioner amplifier assembly and each servo are connected by the air conditioner harness assembly. The air conditioner amplifier assembly supplies power and sends operation command information to each servo through the air conditioner harness assembly. Each servo sends damper position information to the air conditioner amplifier assembly.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Detection Condition</ptxt>
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Diagnosis Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Abnormal Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Malfunction Duration</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B1497/97</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Communication between air conditioner amplifier assembly and each servo is abnormal or stopped</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>10 seconds or more (current malfunction only)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Air conditioner harness assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Air Conditioner Amplifier Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005LM00RX_06" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005LM00RX_07" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000005LM00RX_07_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___0000BZE00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Air Conditioner Amplifier Assembly (BBUS Terminal, BUSGND Terminal)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the air conditioner amplifier assembly connector. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005KW01EX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E144394J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.65in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B2 (BUSG) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the terminals of the air conditioner amplifier assembly connector. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM0000005KW01EX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E144394J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.65in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B4(BBUS) - B2(BUSG)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005LM00RX_07_0005" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000005LM00RX_07_0006" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005LM00RX_07_0005">
<testtitle>Replace Air Conditioner Harness Assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000213F002X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000005LM00RX_07_0006">
<testtitle>Replace Air Conditioner Amplifier Assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002140002X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
